<spell-notebook "visibility theming">
	<header level="1">
		Visibility
		<header>Visibility provides a set of callbacks for when content appears in the viewport.</>
	</>
	<visibility-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			A visibility draws nothing: it's a plain block around its content, with no tokens of its own. Style
			it through `::part(visibility)`, and the images' fade with `animation` and `duration`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-visibility::part(visibility) {
			  min-height: 50vh;
			}
			```
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-visibility" playground>
				<ui-visibility once="false" offset="0">
					<p>I fire <code>ui-in-view</> and <code>ui-out-of-view</> each time I come and go.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>Visibility has no look to restyle.</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
